other Dragon pung with J3\n\nW5 is isolated and doesn't contribute to any strong pattern. Discarding W5 keeps my pairs (W1, T3, T6, J3) and maintains flexibility for both pung and chow formations in the Bamboo suit.\n\nReason: W5 is an isolated tile that doesn't fit into any developing pattern. Keeping it reduces my chances of forming a coherent hand. By discarding W5, I maintain my pairs (W1, T3, T6, J3) and preserve the Bamboo suit connectivity (T3-T5-T6-T7) which can form chows or pungs. This keeps multiple winning paths open while working toward Half Flush (Bamboos + Honors) combined with my existing Dragon pung for at least 8 points.\n\nAnswer: Play W5"}
